# The contract test of the stage ops of md_alg (D[md-alg-stages]): the
# cases of Inputs/md-alg/stages.mlir run once by the serial definitions on
# the host (convert-md-alg-to-scf) and once by the SIMT lowering on a device
# (convert-md-alg-to-gpu), and the outputs compared by each op's contract.
# The counting sort (md_alg.sort_by_key) is ordered: its keys, counts,
# start, cursor, order, and side outputs (a slot of each item and a
# counter) are compared to the bit, in four forms (by a key region of i32
# or index bins, with the op's clear or the caller's, by `by`; by keys
# given, with and without items that have no bin), by every scan and sort
# strategy, and unordered (its bins compared after a canonical sort), on no items, one, 20 in 7 bins, 1,025 in 1,000, 3,000 in 50,
# all 3,000 in one bin (with and without items without a bin), 129 in 129,
# and 5,000 in 3. The appends (md_alg.append) are compared by their counts
# and counter to the bit, and by the checks that the stages.mlir host makes
# against its own lists: no item kept, one, every item of one list of 640
# with room for exactly its 10 blocks, one fewer, and many more, and lists
# that run at once on the device (8 and 40 lists, blocks begun in the
# middle of a warp's round) with room to spare, far too little, and none.
#
# REQUIRES: cuda
#
# RUN: cat %S/Inputs/md-alg/host.mlir %S/Inputs/md-alg/helpers.mlir \
# RUN:     %S/Inputs/md-alg/append-host.mlir %S/Inputs/md-alg/stages.mlir \
# RUN: | mdir-opt --convert-md-alg-to-scf \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils > %t.serial
# RUN: cat %S/Inputs/md-alg/device.mlir %S/Inputs/md-alg/helpers.mlir \
# RUN:     %S/Inputs/md-alg/append-device.mlir %S/Inputs/md-alg/stages.mlir \
# RUN: | mdir-opt --convert-md-alg-to-gpu \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_gpu_to_llvm > %t.simt.mlir
# RUN: mlir-runner %t.simt.mlir -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda > %t.simt
# RUN: diff %t.serial %t.simt
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.simt
# Of the case of 20 items: the orders of A and C, and that of E after its
# canonical sort; then the checks of the nine runs of appends.
# CHECK-COUNT-3: ( 21, {{.*}} )( 13, 15, 9, 14, 1, 3, 17, 19, 0, 2, 6, 11, 7, 8, 12, 18, 10, -7, -7, -7, -7 )
# CHECK: ( 3, {{.*}} )( 0, 1, 1 )
# CHECK: ( 3, {{.*}} )( 1, 1, 1 )
# CHECK: ( 3, {{.*}} )( 10, 1, 1 )
# CHECK: ( 3, {{.*}} )( 9, 1, 0 )
# CHECK: ( 3, {{.*}} )( 10, 1, 1 )
# CHECK: ( 3, {{.*}} )( 24, 1, 1 )
# CHECK: ( 3, {{.*}} )( 3, 1, 0 )
# CHECK: ( 3, {{.*}} )( 76, 1, 1 )
# CHECK: ( 3, {{.*}} )( 0, 1, 0 )
#
# Under compute-sanitizer (with -Dsanitize=1): memcheck and racecheck, for
# the writes past the capacity that the append must not make, the atomics
# of the counts and of the pool, and the warp's shared blocks.
# RUN: %if compute-sanitizer %{ %compute_sanitizer --tool memcheck \
# RUN:     --error-exitcode 1 mlir-runner %t.simt.mlir -e main \
# RUN:     --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MEM %}
# RUN: %if compute-sanitizer %{ %compute_sanitizer --tool racecheck \
# RUN:     --error-exitcode 1 mlir-runner %t.simt.mlir -e main \
# RUN:     --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RACE %}
# MEM: ERROR SUMMARY: 0 errors
# RACE: RACECHECK SUMMARY: 0 hazards displayed (0 errors, 0 warnings)
